# Hierarchical Discourse Graph RAG — Walkthrough

## Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    subgraph "Baseline RAG"
        PDF1["📄 PDF"] --> C1["Chunks"] --> FAISS["FAISS\nVector Store"] --> LLM1["Groq LLM"]
    end

    subgraph "Novel Graph RAG"
        PDF2["📄 PDF"] --> C2["Chunks"]
        C2 --> L1["Layer 1\nInstances"]
        L1 --> L2["Layer 2\nConcepts"]
        L2 --> L3["Layer 3\nCommunities"]
        L1 & L2 & L3 --> NEO["Neo4j"]
        NEO --> HIER["Hierarchical\nRetrieval"]
        HIER --> LLM2["Groq LLM"]
    end

    subgraph "Benchmark"
        LLM1 --> EVAL["📊 Metrics\nComparison"]
        LLM2 --> EVAL
    end
```

## Project Files

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| [config.py](file:///d:/mini2/config.py) | Shared config, loads [.env](file:///d:/mini2/.env) credentials |
| [gen_pdfs.py](file:///d:/mini2/gen_pdfs.py) | Generates 2 small benchmark PDFs |
| [baseline_rag.py](file:///d:/mini2/baseline_rag.py) | Standard RAG: PDF → FAISS → Groq |
| [graph_builder.py](file:///d:/mini2/graph_builder.py) | **Novel**: 3-layer hierarchical graph construction |
| [graph_retriever.py](file:///d:/mini2/graph_retriever.py) | **Novel**: Hierarchical traverse-and-collect retrieval |
| [graph_rag.py](file:///d:/mini2/graph_rag.py) | End-to-end Graph RAG pipeline |
| [questions.json](file:///d:/mini2/questions.json) | 15 benchmark questions (factual/multi-hop/global) |
| [benchmark.py](file:///d:/mini2/benchmark.py) | Runs both pipelines, computes metrics, generates charts |

## What's Novel

1. **3-Layer Graph** — Not a flat entity graph. Instances → Concepts → Communities with LLM-generated summaries
2. **Data-Driven Edges** — Relationship types emerge from data (`improves`, `limited_by`, etc.), not a fixed taxonomy
3. **Top-Down Retrieval** — Community match → Concept drill → Instance BFS, instead of flat vector similarity

## Setup & Run

```bash
# 1. Fill .env with your actual credentials
# 2. Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 3. Generate benchmark PDFs
python gen_pdfs.py

# 4. Test baseline RAG alone
python baseline_rag.py --pdf data/ai_agents.pdf --query "What is ReAct?"

# 5. Build graph + test Graph RAG
python graph_rag.py --pdf data/ai_agents.pdf --build --query "What is ReAct?"

# 6. Full benchmark comparison
python benchmark.py --pdf data/ai_agents.pdf
```

Output in `results/`: `baseline_results.json`, `graphrag_results.json`, `comparison_chart.png`
